{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01UMTBhgY11HDWEkCckFh5mK", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t\"\"\"Rolling window sums over a series of event counts.\n2\t\n3\tA series holds one non-negative count per time step, such as requests\n4\tper second. The sum of each window of consecutive steps is the load\n5\tover that window.\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\t\n8\timport numpy as np\n9\tfrom numpy.typing import NDArray\n10\t\n11\t\n12\tdef rolling_sum(values: NDArray[np.int64], width: int) -> NDArray[np.int64]:\n13\t    \"\"\"Sum every window of ``width`` consecutive values.\n14\t\n15\t    Parameters\n16\t    ----------\n17\t    values : numpy.ndarray of int64, shape (n,)\n18\t        Counts, one per time step. Every window sum must fit in int64.\n19\t    width : int\n20\t        Number of consecutive values in each window, at least 1.\n21\t\n22\t    Returns\n23\t    -------\n24\t    numpy.ndarray of int64, shape (max(n - width + 1, 0),)\n25\t        Element ``i`` is ``values[i:i + width].sum()``. Empty when\n26\t        ``width`` exceeds ``n``.\n27\t\n28\t    Raises\n29\t    ------\n30\t    ValueError"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a734416c-13ce-46ff-97b3-97cd0f39fee4", "uuid": "bcf398d5-1bec-4b2b-91a8-69d47ad1ce34", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T22:14:54.743Z"}
